 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This is my poor heart's life, o'er sixty years,\nThe love I had for thee; it has never\nLoved the wronged heart which cannot,\nAlas! Love him more than you ever.\nYou are good men and have done me many\nFathers and sons not worth the coin given,\nBut I am yours from that first hour\nWhen my arms were bound and fasten'd about,\nMy hands clasped in your fingers, ever\nOft night by night as night upon\nLight to keep the light of our\nSoul together unseen between us,",
